[{"id":"VRCE-2-109-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":1,"english":"When the ascetics had gone away, Rāghava reflected (as to his stay at that place); and from diverse reasons, he did not relish remaining there any further.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.767,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fa3ac0b3705cf49a468d7d50f941c8538838e74a1656f6c34ea2831cf433564","compact":"816fad61e77014b65bfc3e623c58f4da9e490a9f44ed33ce1af3a31768ed93c6","nasal":"69b5004a9e41ed188dbd41725039dde55c274b0a5e1906aba0878cb0fa416d84"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":2,"english":"Here have I seen Bharata and my mother in company with the citizens. Overwhelmed with grief on my account, they ever recur to my memory.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d886d1ced1c29ebf59f5a5d3490b9b8b341895ceaea911b5d4bc79cb32a8b535","compact":"9d39460caf37f1f8fac8ccf6d939ac5e9be659b1853413c15fde80201c03435d","nasal":"5738b46aa907a77076c7dce9fc34c67732aa0c8ddbd7e0b797356580c807c739"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":3,"english":"And in consequence of the troops of that highsouled one having quartered here as well as the dung discharged by his elephants and horses, this place has got exceedingly dirty.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"99de2a4a9026a5c6066de76bdb4bc9d1d48375e3d890b3dc5548e807a80fedd4","compact":"377ce7305d2510645edf11369a8d57d859fb53618225e6f5236e2abb0364e513","nasal":"27b6334b12c40e86cc25c70fa4e1f265c949bfefd2a1419ae0afeae28df64dab"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":4,"english":"Therefore will I go to another quarter. Having settled this in his mind, Rāghava departed along with Videha's daughter and Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1034da904dc3f33727ba5b5009faab72eb3b088add4eaaafae5b064509246a74","compact":"2c78b89a6ec1c4b77e3e0241381f36255023313f6173b9d27627298548abf162","nasal":"ea4a430bf11fabecb1b12d9e71c875709f734a0ae9b0977458b2afd76e33b723"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":5,"english":"And having arrived at Atri's asylum, that renowned one paid obeisance (to the sage); and the reverend Atri also on his pare received Rāma asason.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84d4e8247572daf7868856a96711db36e1757032a85af6b90120b3bf6823f9b3","compact":"f6205a92aaab19ee09ce0896b1851b7581cb11580be2d32a9992e3085e051696","nasal":"353c9b2f569f88da868502bdf6aa5eb188ebca53604eefbff4eefe8bb5657ede"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":6,"english":"And having personally given Rāma respectful reception and entertainment, the ascetic regarded the exalted Lakşmaņa and Sītā with a gracious eye.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b65b5a8f91e45919fbdfa0539284c3a5242e4ec13aa23c0745f18b9d29496e9","compact":"40b61e91928c56e801c293fd03144a90abe14553c4960909cce5556c7f53d1d7","nasal":"c7e301ab92360e768fefd4c59f9e3e1bdf563818d98303e071c47cccd7c6736c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":7,"english":"And his aged wife having come there, Atri greeted her; and after she had been paid homage, the sage cognizant of virtue ever engaged in the good of all creatures, gladdened her (by presenting Sītā to her.) And that best of sages said to the pious female ascetic, Anasüyā, engaged in offices of virtue, “Do you accept Videha's daughter.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"56df96718a0fc852f253fddc0b6bc71c096897cb36dc9bc585286d9c7562c148","compact":"8f035373c04a69b74ef27d1f3f9d426e35245479f19b8ec29aca9de4d8518b5c","nasal":"c704cdf082829ca4765c8c56fb9f2e329a3f77ab68f2438610f4aa6201b8768e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":8,"english":"And his aged wife having come there, Atri greeted her; and after she had been paid homage, the sage cognizant of virtue ever engaged in the good of all creatures, gladdened her (by presenting Sītā to her.) And that best of sages said to the pious female ascetic, Anasüyā, engaged in offices of virtue, “Do you accept Videha's daughter.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"252245d55af05b677e85c5184f77a574cbd0fd1b10e73bf316a93be72608ebb6","compact":"e70ba97c206ba4b5f1e9f5e4aa75cc075de638c702c4d401b3393fcfcb270f99","nasal":"50fa753769515422f1fbce9c4f74c8a75774a82fdace096b7fdc3f53059bebc0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":9,"english":"And Atri related to Rāma matters connected with the female ascetic, engaged in offices of virtue, The people were ceaselessly burning in consequence of a drought extending over ten years. O sinless one, that one resembling your mother is this, by whom furnished with rigid asceticism and adorned with voluntary penances, were created fruits and roots and the Jāhnavi was made to flow through the asylum; by whom were performed mighty austerities for ten thousand years, in virtue of whose pen ances, disturbances to the asceticism of the sages ceased, by whom ten nights were brought within the compass of a single one.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.646,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86711580a5f98a0fe1793a659059986ba0bd56bf7cf70926ef4edc750fc234d0","compact":"6e92413006a3cf3ce0f9705ab6f9328f99edd7b0c5d9f60c1aad3c9bd92793ba","nasal":"15eb6edf823dc0191ffc9d51e4adeeaf2c4d585b6ed0babe016ec2799877d792"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":10,"english":"And Atri related to Rāma matters connected with the female ascetic, engaged in offices of virtue, The people were ceaselessly burning in consequence of a drought extending over ten years. O sinless one, that one resembling your mother is this, by whom furnished with rigid asceticism and adorned with voluntary penances, were created fruits and roots and the Jāhnavi was made to flow through the asylum; by whom were performed mighty austerities for ten thousand years, in virtue of whose pen ances, disturbances to the asceticism of the sages ceased, by whom ten nights were brought within the compass of a single one.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2027d5b44383ec66f5b8cf78565d313b57ea6b4d6f1a37018000e9d5195a5a5","compact":"795cc5f6b23bf50be2cf1167aa20a612f2dfd6040ac71a6f499a96238d7af381","nasal":"795cc5f6b23bf50be2cf1167aa20a612f2dfd6040ac71a6f499a96238d7af381"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":11,"english":"And Atri related to Rāma matters connected with the female ascetic, engaged in offices of virtue, The people were ceaselessly burning in consequence of a drought extending over ten years. O sinless one, that one resembling your mother is this, by whom furnished with rigid asceticism and adorned with voluntary penances, were created fruits and roots and the Jāhnavi was made to flow through the asylum; by whom were performed mighty austerities for ten thousand years, in virtue of whose pen ances, disturbances to the asceticism of the sages ceased, by whom ten nights were brought within the compass of a single one.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86af2ca827c8c7d93abe0d6c13a47dd6058e0d9094e45b7b69e53fc968f2b2a3","compact":"30139cb1ba294cea9860069ec145cde46dc4e327b52eb343583b07349f10b149","nasal":"30139cb1ba294cea9860069ec145cde46dc4e327b52eb343583b07349f10b149"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":12,"english":"And Atri related to Rāma matters connected with the female ascetic, engaged in offices of virtue, The people were ceaselessly burning in consequence of a drought extending over ten y