hī, who is worthy of being served both in this world and the next, and who is like imperishable asceticism.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e93b8e6f5a3e46be88d91b03e0daf2f7e1054c94e7a19ef819b0f69b791bacdf","compact":"493ea6f93437a5c34c2041e7d2bf87b6ac7ef46420017c7b2898bafa2f9682fe","nasal":"806605f72eb0c0e93f05e4b23982ae441ab7844e45c9118b02764a527a2c299f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":26,"english":"But bad women whose hearts hunger after carnality, and who lord over their husbands, do not get acquainted with the virtues and demerits (of their husbands); and range at their will.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6caaa4f5245c3d913cb77b4ca5add5d187ce306d426c87acbd7ce647d5791fa3","compact":"af4fc991fcdc42afe653e0cc9c55526154b3bbd5d809517358400637bfddf387","nasal":"e51305620d0a3935cea07bf6c0fa8500cb98cdbf2537f9ecc0e99c6c583be141"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-109-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":109,"verse":27,"english":"O Mithilā's daughter, surely women of this sort who are given to doing evil acts, reap infamy and fall off from righteousness.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-117-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2109027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"345748ab05c78fdc569ca9e13e1e30e644c560c8afa2305e44c1aec3913b9150","compact":"ca938ca0b3c44f4502e8cc0fa855740a9dd8e3fe34165c0925a2dd6723ad21a2","nasal":"49702c830c5